At the annual meeting of Zhejiang University, the students played a leading role, and the research results made people's brains open.
Use the air to wash your hands, guise to judge the disease and accurately search for the source of smog Last night, at the opening ceremony of the 2016 academic conference of Zhejiang University, a series of brain-opening academic achievements were commended.
The main researchers of these results are students, the study covers the environment, machinery, energy, health care, life sciences, humanities education and other major fields, students start from a curious idea and create a lot of high-end inventions with application value, some of the projects have been won in the domestic and international awards.
Biosensors: your family medical examiner
Zhang Diming, a doctoral student in the School of Biomedical Engineering, demonstrated a biosensor on a smartphone end that is only half the size of a smartphone.
"You only need to take a gentle breath, this set of instruments from the composition of the gas you exhale, the initial detection of physical health."
Zhang Liming said that the sensor is connected to the smartphone, and after exhaling the gas, the health report will be displayed on the mobile phone.
Smart bracelets that can detect health conditions on the market generally detect physical parameters such as temperature and pulse.
This set of bio-sensors uses graphene as a new type of material, and its target is chemical elements, and the keen sense of smell allows it to reflect the health of the body in a deeper and more accurate way.
Smart Surgical Lights: Doctor's high-energy eyes
In addition to smart phones, intelligent surgical lights are also used in the operating room.
This invention won the silver medal at this year’s 44th International Invention Exhibition in Geneva, Switzerland.
Zhu Linjing, a master's student in the School of Optoelectronics Science and Engineering, opened a new idea in the shortcomings of traditional surgical lamps and invented intelligent LED surgery shadowless lamps.
"A lot of the early detection of the disease is not in place, it is related to the doctor's operating room lights."
Shen Junfei said, for example, in the early detection of cancer, if the doctor can not see all the tumor tissue in time, then the cancer cells will spread.
This kind of intelligent surgical lamp has four lamp discs, by adjusting the spectrum, to enhance the difference between different tissues in the light.
In the course of the operation, the doctor can adjust the size, brightness, spectra, color uniformity, and shadow-free rate at any time according to surgical needs and personal habits.
This kind of intelligent surgical lamp has been tested in hospitals such as Shao Yifu Hospital affiliated with Zhejiang University School of Medicine and Children's Hospital of Zhejiang University School of Medicine to obtain better feedback.
In October last year, this invention won the first prize of the National Challenge Cup.
Wash your hands with the air: save the water and cool
Ordinary people's hands wash their hands with water, at the most rinsing soap, squeezing hand sanitizer, and Li Qizhang and other students have invented a set of "air hand-washing devices".
As long as we are standing on a hand-washing station, our body weight can compress the air.
“It’s just like a pneumatic.
The compressed air forms a fluid at the faucet, where the water binds together.
That way, we'll be able to wash our hands!"
The color rendering reaction and bacterial residue experiments have shown that the effect of hand washing through this method is the same as that of ordinary handwashing methods.
This device only needs to rely on our own gravity to drive, both to ensure the degree of washing, but also to save 90% of the water, the whole process is completely free of energy consumption, energy saving and environmental protection.
Last year, at the 2nd Global Grand Summit, the invention stood out among the world’s top universities and received its only gold award.
