First of all, I personally believe that "four seas" is an all-round rotten film, in every sense.
But you have to say that the film is not a bright spot, that is not at least the soundtrack selection is very good.
There are many kinds of rotten pieces, so that you can fall asleep in the movie theater, let you look at the indignant is also a kind, "four seas" for the audience is like a monkey on Emei Mountain, it can ignite your anger in countless ways.
When it comes to insulting the spectators, Han Han is really talented.
The most painful thing in this film is that it seems to be a creature in a Ke family novel, it is indescribable, and there are many loopholes, just like the windbreaker on the little brother.
Even after watching it, you will wonder if there is a director's implied metaphor, but when you think about it, you find that it is actually a piece of shit.
Let’s start with a few things that are difficult for me to understand.
The man's main residence should be on a small island in the south, and his grandmother was dependent on each other.
Her grandmother had a desire to see the snow, and then arranged for a gentleman in the neighborhood to send her to the northeast to see the snow in a small van.
The old man in the van from the south to the northeast to see the snow?
He and his father were very worried about this.
The old man did not go down there.
How to open a hotel on an abandoned ship, how did the woman's brother get a business license?
Why can the island's flying car party bastards easily cut a part of the mountain road to the road?
Then the truck in the middle of the road was parked on the side of the road, and even the truck driver could not be found around.
The feeling of this tool is also too obvious.
Why would a mixed-flying car party, which is ill-recognizable and suspected, become an auxiliary police officer?
In the face of usury, why do not call the police, the police in the film also specifically asked whether there are any difficulties?
An adult knows how to use a smartphone, but he does not know how to open the door with a room card in the hotel, and then forcibly arrange not to find a hotel owner to sit and sleep outside the room.
Such inexplicable plots permeate the entire film, because the plot is so outrageous that it makes me miserable when I recall them.
In addition to the plot, what is even worse is the main theme of the film, or that the film has no main theme at all, it is an abominable suture.
At the beginning of the film, you will think that he wants to make a comedy, more than 20 minutes later, you guess that it may be a motivational film, when you look at it, you think it may be a drama film that does not want to reflect the survival of young people in a small town.
In fact, for most people, they are also very familiar with all kinds of movies, for example, if you want to shoot a motorcyclist, it is motivation + comedy and then tell the audience how a gifted rookie is becoming successful.
If you want to make love movies, then you can honestly say that you like to ride a motorbike in a small-town youth and a waiter's femininity.
If you want to reflect the reality, then at the very least your plot can’t come up with something contrary to the normal world.
(For example, Yin's new motorbike has just been burned, and can still sing the role), you can't open some brain holes that even Kennedy can't see.
As for the fact that the hostess is obviously not mentally retarded in some aspects, like a 5-year-old child, I really don't know if this is the cause of acting or the director's request.
I don't understand why Han Han, as a racing driver, is so keen to add crash plots in his own films?
This kind of film is arranged in the Spring Festival file, is it in order to plug the audience?
