Education: What does it take to save a kidnapped child?
If there is an analogy with the famous public service advertising slogan of "there is no killing without buying and selling", then in a good environment where there is no "abduction" demand, group prevention and group governance, the whole people's anti-abduction, so that the abduction behavior is unprofitable, the risk is high, and the cost is high, and this kind of crime will not happen again and again.
Recently, the Criminal Investigative Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security launched an emergency release platform for the release of information on children's disappearances developed by the Criminal Investigative Office of the Ministry of Public
This is an Internet information platform created to establish an authoritative channel for the release of information on the disappearance of children and the timely recovery of abducted children.
I heard that this app is called "reunion" and it's full of warmth.
New technological means is not only the name of "literary art", full of feelings, and the use of informatization properly, practical and effective.
The primary goal is to recover the abducted children and protect their personal safety and freedom.
The second is the trial and punishment of the suspects.
The meaning of criminal punishment, from individual punishment, social prevention to legal education, can enumerate a lot of "big words".
However, priority should be given to the personal safety of the victims before the trafficking case is solved.
Under the urgent purpose of â€œseeking help â€œstitution for helpâ€ , there are many different and controversial topics such as â€œwhether the abduction of children should always be subject to the death penaltyâ, which can be put on hold and discuss carefully; but the matter of rescuing abducted children cannot.
According to the experience of the investigation of such cases, human traffickers are used to stay away from the crime scene as soon as possible.
One more than a minute of delay, the child may be further away from the parents, and the difficulty of the detection of the case will be increased by one point.
In this case, it is indeed a pragmatic action to come up with an effective method such as the "reunification" platform that directly contributes to the detection of cases and the recovery of children.
After all, â€œabductionâ€ is a big task that needs to be done by operating the entire legal system.
To combat crime and protect the rights and interests of children and parents, from the improvement of legislation to the protection of the judiciary, as well as the meticulousness of law enforcement, there is no need to carry out the care of "child protection and weak".
In addition, the prevention of child trafficking can be done better, from the family to the society.
For example, in a common case, a family of three is resting at the train station, their parents are asleep, and they wake up to find that the child is missing.
A two-year-old should not be expected to have sufficient self-preservation skills, but as a parent of a young child, it should have at least a considerable sense of protection.
Both parents take turns to rest, or to put the child under safe protection, which is the most basic means to prevent the abduction of a child.
Judging from the other side of the police's efforts to combat the crime of human trafficking, the purchase of abducted children should also be paid attention and punished.
Individual wrongful acts are often only a link in a long chain.
According to China's Criminal Law, the statutory penalty for the crime of trafficking in children is 5 years; if the circumstances are particularly serious, the death penalty and the confiscation of property.
Under the general trend of â€œlendiversionâ€, the crime of trafficking in children is obviously a more serious crime.
So far, there are still many trafficking cases every year.
It can be seen that some people are backward in the concept of raising children, and the legal awareness is weak.
The legal education of this part of the people should be followed up simultaneously.
In order to effectively control the crime of trafficking, we must not rely solely on official and strict law enforcement.
If the "market" is widely available, the abductors want to fry, constantly innovate the means of trafficking, and form a "fight law" situation with law enforcers, the abduction action is bound to fall into an inefficient quagmire.
Therefore, the elimination of backward concepts and the popularization of legal common sense will also also contribute to the eradication of the crime of trafficking and the purchase of children.
