Jiangxi will train tens of thousands of rural primary school sound and beauty teachers within 3 years - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Nanchang, May 22 (Reporter Chen Yushan) The reporter recently learned from the Jiangxi Provincial Department of Education that in order to enhance the guarantee capacity of the shortage of discipline teachers and achieve the balanced development of compulsory education in rural areas, since 2016, Jiangxi Province's three-year plan has taken three years to train qualified music, fine arts and physical education teachers in the province's villages (townships and below), with a total of 10,000.
It is understood that the purpose of this training for Jiangxi province's rural primary schools under the age of 45 with music, fine arts, sports knowledge base or talents, can also serve as music, fine arts, physical education courses of other subject teachers.
Through training, enable them to master the basic knowledge and teaching skills of the teaching of sound and aesthetic disciplines, update teaching ideas and concepts, master modern teaching methods, improve the teaching ability of the subject, activity design ability, campus cultural ability and self-development ability, build a team of multi-disciplinary and multi-energy sound and beauty teachers, and alleviate the lack of problems of rural sound and beauty teachers.
In order to ensure the quality and effectiveness of the training, Jiangxi is also planned to train for music, fine arts and physical education in 100 counties (cities and districts) in the province, with a total of 300 trainees to comprehensively enhance their teaching and demonstration leadership capabilities, teaching and research activity design and organization capabilities, training capabilities, and network training workshops, and play the role of teaching, demonstration, guidance and supervision.
