The 18th “World Beverage Innovation Awards” is an award jointly organized by FoodBev Media in conjunction with Brau Beviale in Nuremberg, Germany.
It attracted 279 entries from 22 different categories from 25 countries.
On October 15, the list of finalists will be announced, and the list of the final winners will be announced online on November 11.
We have seen that the LP28 sugar-free yoghurt of Yuanqi Forest was shortlisted for the best milk beverage award, the "GOGO Wuhan" marketing of Yili Amushi was shortlisted for the best marketing campaign, and Pepsi and People's Daily new media cooperation packaging were also shortlisted for the best packaging design / label award.
Laura Nettle, senior director of marketing at FoodBev Media, said: “We’re excited to celebrate the 18th year of the annual World Beverage Innovation Award with Brau Beviale.
From new flavors, new concepts and new features to brands, packaging and manufacturing, we are seeing trends in the beverage industry as the industry continues to innovate in a more sustainable way.
The World Beverage Innovation Award recognises new and existing brands in the global beverage industry with the most ambitious new products and developments of this year.
Below is a complete list of finalists in each category.
Technology developed by Ardagh Group can re-melt 100% recycled glass into a new bottle.
The box is 100% recyclable, which can reduce packaging by 66% and reduce carbon emissions by 97%.
LatCub is 100% biodegradable, uses less paper, and doesn’t use environmentally harmful glue or tape.
Technology developed by Ardagh Group to re-melt 100% recycled glass into a new bottle.
The final list of winners will be announced on FoodBev Media's YouTube channel on November 11 (British daylight saving time), and the FBIF will continue to report for you.
