Iran's president: if sanctions against Iran are lifted, an agreement is expected to be reached - Xinhua News Agency
TEHRAN, Dec. 11 (Xinhua) -- Iranian President Lehi said in the Iranian capital Tehran on the 11th that if the United States lifts sanctions on Iran, the negotiation of a comprehensive agreement on the Iranian nuclear issue can reach a "good agreement."
According to the news released by the Iranian president's website on the same day, Lehi said at a meeting with Iran's neighboring countries on the same day that by submitting proposals to other relevant parties to the Iranian nuclear agreement, Iran has proved the sincerity of its negotiations.
If the U.S. side is determined, "the road to an agreement will be smooth."
The relevant parties to the Iranian nuclear agreement began to hold talks in the Austrian capital Vienna in April this year to discuss the resumption of compliance between the United States and Iran.
The new round of talks began in Vienna on November 29, adjourned temporarily on December 3 and continued on December 9.
