Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory letter to the Greater Bay Area Science Forum in 2021 - Xinhua
BEIJING, Dec. 11 (Xinhua) -- On December 11, President Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory letter to the Greater Bay Area Science Forum in 2021.
Xi Jinping pointed out that today's world is experiencing great changes that have not been seen for a hundred years, global scientific and technological innovation has entered a period of intense activity, and a new round of scientific and technological revolution and industrial change has had a profound impact on the global economic structure.
The Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area should focus on the strategic positioning of building an international scientific and technological innovation center, strive to build a global highland of scientific and technological innovation, and promote the development of emerging industries.
China is willing to work with scientists and international scientific and technological organizations around the world to strengthen international scientific and technological exchanges and cooperation, strengthen research on major scientific issues, promote common scientific and technological cracking, deepen cooperation in key scientific projects, and jointly promote the development of the world's scientific undertakings to better benefit mankind.
The 2021 Greater Bay Area Science Forum opened on the same day in Guangzhou, Guangdong Province with the theme of "exploring the future, sharing science", hosted by the Guangdong Provincial People's Government.
