Guangxi college students can stay off for up to 5 years of entrepreneurship - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Nanning, May 19 (Reporter Zhang Ying) The reporter recently learned from the Education Department of Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region that in the future, Guangxi colleges and universities will implement a flexible education system to relax the student's respite period, and the number of years of entrepreneurship in school students can be extended by 2 to 5 years on the basis of the original academic system.
In order to promote the entrepreneurship and innovation ability of college students, Guangxi education, human society and other departments work together to build an entrepreneurship platform, the construction of more out-of-university practice teaching bases, university science and technology parks, college student entrepreneurship parks, entrepreneurship incubation bases, etc., to provide an external guarantee for college entrepreneurship.
According to the requirements, by 2020, the area of innovation and entrepreneurship practice bases in colleges and universities should reach more than 3,000 square meters for undergraduate schools, and higher vocational schools should reach more than 2,000 square meters.
The government encourages colleges and universities to set up innovation and entrepreneurship credits, giving priority to supporting students with outstanding performance in innovation and entrepreneurship practice.
At least two months every two years, college teachers need to exercise in industry enterprises, so as to improve the awareness and ability of teachers in innovation and entrepreneurship education.
The education department of the autonomous region requires Guangxi colleges and universities to implement in-depth innovation and entrepreneurship training programs for college students, and strives to enable every college student to participate in an innovation and entrepreneurship training program during the school period.
Universities should actively organize students to participate in all kinds of innovation and entrepreneurship competitions at all levels, and provide financial support.
NEWS GOV-MO: The University of Australia awarded honorary doctorates to 7 luminaries
The University of Macau today (11th) held an "Official Award Ceremony for Honorary Degrees and Advanced Degrees in 2021" to award honorary doctorates to Liu Zunyi, Chen Kaixian, Nakamura, Li Lanjuan, Li Yiliang and Jiang Chaohui in recognition of their outstanding achievements and their significant contribution to the development of society and education in recognition of their outstanding achievements and their significant contributions to the development of society and education.
At the awarding ceremony, the Chief Executive and the Superintendent of the University of Australia and the Director of the Social and Cultural Affairs Department Ouyang Yu awarded the honorary doctoral degree accompanied by Lin Jincheng, President of the Council of the University of Australia, and Song Yonghua, President of the Australian University.
Professor Liu Zunyi was awarded an honorary doctorate in education, Professor Chen was awarded an honorary doctorate in science and economics by Professor Chen Xixian was awarded an honorary doctorate in science and economics, Professor Li Lanjuan was awarded an honorary doctorate in science and technology, Professor Li Liliang was awarded an honorary doctorate in business administration, Professor Zhu Lilan was awarded an honorary doctorate in science, and Ms. Jiang Chaohui was awarded an honorary doctorate in science.
In his speech, Ou Yangyu first expressed his warm congratulations to the seven outstanding people who were awarded the honorary doctoral degree, expressed their warm congratulations and paid high tribute, they have made extraordinary achievements in different fields and made excellent contributions to the development of the country and the progress of the world; at the same time, Ouyang Yu expressed their most sincere wishes to the graduates and parents, and also paid sincere tribute to the dedicated and academic staff of the university.
Sun Yifeng, a lecture professor at the College of Humanities of the University of Australia, said that Professor Liu Zunyi is a world-renowned economist who is known for his outstanding academic achievements and forward-looking educational philosophy.
In addition to his achievements in the fields of economic development, economic growth and the economy of East Asia, he is also a visionary educational leader.
In short, he has made outstanding achievements in many fields.
Sun Yifeng, when he read the second paternity speech, said that Professor Nauchura is a pioneer in sustainable energy technology.
He became one of the three winners of the 2014 Nobel Prize in Physics for his invention of the blue light-emitting diode (LED).
Professor Nakamura's invention has not only revolutionized the lighting industry, but also promoted the creation of white light-emitting diodes, which are now widely used in daily life and industrial production, making a great contribution to the well-being of mankind.
When Sun Yifeng read Li Lanjuan's speech, he said that as a pioneer of China's artificial liver industry, Professor Li Lanjuan has created a unique and effective artificial liver system, and has made a major breakthrough in the treatment of heavy hepatitis liver failure, which has significantly reduced the case fatality rate of liver failure.
In the fight against the new crown of pneumonia, the "four anti-two balance" program proposed by her and the team and the three major technologies of artificial liver, microecology and stem cells have significantly improved the rate of critical care.
Sun Yifeng said that Professor Li Yiliang has laid the foundation for the innovative study of operation and management, shaped the way of supply chain theory and practice, and revolutionized business models around the world.
Li is known for popularizing the concept of long whip effects in operations management and exploring measures to deal with this phenomenon.
Nowadays, under the epidemic and tense economic situation in various countries, the long whip effect has become more and more prominent, causing serious damage to the supply chain.
Li Xiliang's far-of-the-sighted research, such as sending charcoal in the snow, has helped the industry cope with difficulties and thus bring huge social value.
In her scientific research work, she discovered a ground-breaking and innovative dyeing technology for the preparation of samples and enjoys a high reputation among domestic and foreign scientific and technological peers.
With extraordinary scientific and technological achievements, she has won important honorary titles such as academicians of the International Eurasian Academy of Sciences, and has won the prestigious status of the world's scientific and technological shrine with her brilliance.
Chen Xin, the acting dean of the Chinese Medical Research Institute of the University of Australia, said that Professor Chen has been engaged in drug research and development for more than 40 years, and his outstanding scientific achievements, as well as his important contributions to the state, the University of Macau, the University of Macau and the national key laboratory, make it have a high international status and prestige.
His positive role in promoting the development of traditional Chinese medicine in Macao and the Greater Bay Area fully reflects his sense of mission of dedication to the national medical development strategy.
The dean of the Australian Institute of Science and Technology said that Ms. Jiang Chaohui's major inventions and patents involved in research and development have so far accumulated more than 15 items related to storage virtualization, navigation, file system and power management, all of which are of high practicality and widely used to enhance the convenience of human life.
As an accomplished inventor, Ms. Jiang is often able to simplify high-level science, technology and theorization and popularization of the public.
In the end, Chen Kaixian, as an honorary Ph.D. representative, read the thank-you speech.
He is pleased to see that the pharmaceutical industry in Macao and the Greater Bay Area has set a good example: from the first national key laboratory of Chinese medicine quality research established by the University to the vigorous development of traditional Chinese medicine in the Greater Bay Area, the university has played a great role in integrating outstanding talents in the field of traditional Chinese medicine in the Greater Bay Area.
In addition, he believes that the University's management team has the vision to not only provide fertile ground for scientific research for students academically, but at the same time for the community to convey a lot of responsible talents.
He was honored to engage in exchanges and cooperation with the University, and expressed his sincere congratulations on Australia's achievements in recent years.
