In the new year, the first thing to do is to summarize the 2022 tactical layout.
It’s about “doing the things right.”
The strategy consists in “doing the right thing” and doing the right thing.
The strategy is to find the direction, the tactic lies in the landing, and on top of most tactical thinking, there is room for strategic thinking.
For example, how to increase the number of customers (tactical thinking), you can think about whether it will continue to deepen in the current field or expand horizontally (strategy thinking); for example, to improve customer retention (tactical thinking), you can think about how to improve the retention rate of core customers and high-value customers (strategic thinking); on the improvement of activity participation (tactical thinking), you can consider how to set the right activity KPI to achieve the right activity goals, such as improving customer engagement, activation of high-value silent customers, and accurately.
Twelve years after its birth, Bitcoin ushered in several landmark events in 2021.
On September 7, the small Central American country of El Salvador designated Bitcoin as legal tender, which is the first time that Bitcoin has become the legal tender of a country or region.
On October 12, for the first time in eight years, the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission approved ProShares to launch a bitcoin ETF and its listing on the New York Stock Exchange, marking the landing of the first compliant bitcoin futures ETF into the U.S. capital market and the expansion of cryptocurrency investment exposure again.
From the point of view of the development of blockchain technology, Bitcoin is not the protagonist.
On November 14, 2021, Bitcoin carried out a soft fork upgrade called “Taproot”, which improved the anonymity of transactions on the Bitcoin network and reduced the data burden in transactions by changing the data structure of the blocks themselves.
