In September 2020, Mr. Lu learned from the housing agent a factory building located in Yuyao Zhuting Town in Zhejiang Province, after seeing the house on the spot many times, Mr. Lu decided to buy the plant.
In December of the same year, Mr. Lu held consultations on the details of the purchase of the plant with Lin, the family member of the owner of the house, and made a deposit of 200,000 yuan through bank transfer on the same day.
"If the buyer does not want to buy this plant, this deposit belongs to the seller, if the seller is not willing to sell the plant, if the seller is not willing to sell the plant, the deposit will be doubled back to the seller, and the two sides agreed to sign the plant sales contract within a week."
However, the two sides failed to form an unanimity due to the main contract terms such as the sale scope of the plant and the payment method, resulting in delays in the signing of the housing sales contract.
Considering that the two sides failed to reach a consensus on the content of the contract, a few days later, Lin returned the deposit of 200,000 yuan to Mr. Lu.
It's hard to look at the house, the deposit is paid, the house price is also ready, it's a "finish door" to sign the contract, but the seller does not sell it, which makes Mr. Lu helpless and angry.
To this end, Mr. Lu sued Lin to the Yuyao Municipal People's Court.
After the trial, the court held that the two sides eventually failed to sign a formal contract, which could not only be attributed to the defendant, and should reasonably be presumed to have failed in consultation, so the deposit penalty should not be applied in this case, and the defendant did not have to bear the liability for breach of the double return of the deposit.
After the first judgment, the plaintiff appealed.
Recently, the second-instance court upheld the verdict.
[Counsel's Reminder] We must exercise the necessary due diligence obligations in the course of the transaction.
At the time of signing the contract, the buyer must exercise the necessary due diligence obligations, for example, to verify the relevant information such as information about the owner of the house and whether the house has been occupied, and to clarify the specific time and place of delivery in the contract to prevent disputes between the two parties during the performance of the contract.
At the end of the "Democracy Summit" on Friday, a spokesperson for the Chinese Foreign Ministry issued a statement on Saturday (December 11), saying that the U.S. holding the "Leadership Summit on Democracy" is to "demonstrate and weaponize democracy in the name of anti-Democracy, incite separatism and confrontation and deflect domestic contradictions."
"For a long time, the United States imposed its own political system and values on others, carried out "democratic transformation", indiscriminately imposed unilateral sanctions, instigated "color revolutions", with disastrous consequences.
"Democracy" has long been the "weapons of weapons of mass destruction" of the United States to interfere in other countries.
The summit was Biden’s move to deliver on his campaign promises.
The two-day meeting took place by video, with the participation of leaders from 111 countries around the world, including the leaders of Taiwan, but China and Russia were not invited.
On the eve of the summit, China and Russia slammed the United States with the emergence of the United States' own democratic problems, saying that the United States was not qualified to host such a summit.
There have also been doubts in the United States at the international level, such as those who have been invited, including leaders with authoritarian tendencies, such as those in the Philippines, Poland, and Brazil, who have suspected that the Biden administration's real intention was not to organize the summit for democracy but for geopolitical purposes.
German Chancellor Scholz also participated in the video democracy summit.
China's Foreign Ministry said in a statement on Saturday that "Today's American-style democracy has become more and more sick, money politics, identity politics, partisan antagonisms, political polarization, social tearing, racial contradictions, and the division of the rich and the poor," and that democracy in the United States is based on the "game of the rich" based on capital.
â€œAs the leaders of our government, we have a responsibility to listen to our citizens, to harden the guardrails of democracy, to push for reforms, to achieve transparent accountable governance that is more resilient to the buffers and shocks of autocracy, as well as those who want to pursue power naked before the public interest.
"Democracy doesn't take it for granted," he said. "We have to constantly update it in every generation, and in my view it's the defining challenge of our time," he said.
Biden also said that global democracy and human rights "negotiations need to be championed in the face of persistent and worrying challenges."
The U.S. has pledged a one-on-year, $424.4 million initiative to strengthen democracy around the world and provide support to independent news media after the Democracy Summit.
The U.S. wants countries to make concrete and public commitments ahead of a physical democracy summit scheduled for the end of 2022 to improve their democracy.
â€œLet all of us live up to our commitments and report on the progress we have made next year,â€ Biden said.
