Qinghai Lake bare carp resource reserves increased by 0.71 million tons this year - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Xining, December 11 (Reporter Luo Xiaofei, Zhang Hongxiang) The reporter learned from the Qinghai Provincial Department of Agriculture and Rural Affairs that the latest monitoring results show that Qinghai Lake's bare carp resources increased by 0.71 million tons this year from the previous year, reaching 108,500 tons, a cumulative increase of more than 40 times compared with the early days of protection in 2002.
Qinghai Lake naked carp commonly known as â€œpricotfishâ€ is a precious fish species unique in Qinghai Lake and plays an important role in maintaining the safety and biodiversity of the ecological chain of â€œwater-fish-birdsâ€ in Qinghai Lake Basin.
In the 1960s and 1970s, due to factors such as the increasing environmental degradation of artificially large-scale hunting and killing of naked carp breeding waters, the number of naked carp in Qinghai Lake plummeted sharply, and the amount of bare carp resources in Qinghai Lake in 2002 was only 2,592 tons.
The naked carp of Qinghai Lake was listed as an endangered species in the "Red List of Chinese Species" in 2004.
Since 2003, Qinghai Province has banned any units, collectives and individuals from catching naked carp in major rivers and tributaries of Qinghai Lake and the lake area, and prohibiting the sale of naked carpes and their products.
At the same time, through measures such as artificial proliferation and release and cleaning up Qinghai Lake's main rivers and rivers into the lake, and designing a scientific and reasonable "fish channel" continue to increase protection, the amount of bare carp resources in Qinghai Lake has been increasing year by year.
Yang Lin, deputy director of the Qinghai Provincial Department of Agriculture and Rural Affairs, said that as of now, Qinghai Lake bare carp has accumulatively implemented nearly 180 million tail, contributing more than 23% to the recovery of bare carp resources.
Qinghai Sanjiangyuan area is an important ecological barrier and water conservation area in China and even in Asia, while Qinghai Lake is a natural barrier and ecological functional area to control the spread of desertification in the west to the east.
In order to protect the ecological environment of the Sanjiangyuan area and the waters of Qinghai Lake, the protection of aquatic wild animals, and maintain the biodiversity of the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau, this year, Qinghai has successively issued a circular on the prohibition of fishing in the key waters of the Yangtze River, the Yellow River and Qinghai Lake, and has built a comprehensive no-capture management system.
