I would like to express my sincere gratitude to my friends for their humanitarian assistance over a long period of more than 30 years after the death of our loved ones, especially since my personal appeal to friends at home and abroad has not been interrupted.
At present, the old parents of the vast majority of the victims have died, and the orphans have also grown into employment.
It’s your actions that have helped these struggling families through the most difficult times.
At present, the new crown epidemic is raging around the world, and the majority of donors have retired.
Therefore, I earnestly ask you to suspend the humanitarian donation to the Tian'anmen mother's group, which should have come to a perfect end.
I will always remember your love, and I firmly believe that your actions will be remembered for history.
For a variety of reasons, I can only express my wishes in this way and ask my friends to understand!
Please accept my sincere blessings.
Let’s take this opportunity to give a brief introduction to the 32-year-long history of humanitarian relief at IFCSS (IFCSS) and the Minnesota-China Foundation for Democracy (MCDF).
In the process of engaged in humanitarian assistance, the National Self-Love Federation and the Minnesota China Foundation for Democracy are two parallel organizations, and the executors of the project are often intersected.
(Apple's Daily image: Tian'an 親網站 is taken care of by 陶業負負負負責). pic.twitter.com/UxID9ZGjzm
Relief funds are often unable to be successfully delivered to June Fourth.
In 1994, Professor Ding suggested that a special group be set up by the "Tiananmen mother" to coordinate and responsible for the reception and distribution of relief funds.
In 1998, MCDF set up the "June Fourth Orphan Education Fund", 11 years after the implementation, in 2009, after the graduation of all orphans, MCDF then set up the "June Fourth Orphaned Elderly special hardship fund", which has been implemented to this day.
Funding for these projects comes mainly from campus and social donations from June Fourth, generous contributions from individuals, and supported by fraternal university’s Democracy Foundation.
Since 2018, it has also received support from the Labor Reform Research Foundation.
Until last year, after a lapse of 31 years, the victims of June Fourth finally received a partial donation from Hong Kong in the name of June Fourth.
During this period, Human Rights in China has also independently implemented their humanitarian assistance programs.
We understand that Mr. Ding's suspension of the June 4 donation is for the donor's consideration, we are indeed some pensioners, the income is not as abundant as before retirement, I would like to express my gratitude to Teacher Ding's "to a friend" letter.
“We will honor our decision to end the project within two years and resume it as soon as necessary.”
We would like to express our gratitude and homage to those who have insisted on generosity and risking the delivery of humanitarian aid for many years.
