If you plan to enter this industry, you can choose to find a place for training, but if there is no idea in this area, it is best to self-study, after all, the training will cost a lot of money, and it will take 6 months to learn.
However, training is indeed a very good choice, especially for those who have self-control and their weakness, training is a very good choice.
If their self-control is relatively strong, you can also choose self-study, but it will be more tired.
Of course, it is very important to choose a good training institution.
First of all, it is necessary to pay attention to the teacher strength of this institution, if the teacher strength is not strong enough, this training institution will have no meaning, of course, some of the newly opened training institutions teachers are not particularly strong.
The second is to explore this training institution before you choose, it is best to explore the students of this institution, after all, only the students of the institution know how this institution is, and the courses explained are good or bad.
In fact, I don't even know how to answer this question, because you don't make a certain introduction to your own situation, and it has a lot to do with learning this thing and the individual's own situation.
Profession, your age, the language you want to learn, and even in which the city will have something to do with the industry you’re studying or trying to work for.
If you are a student and have not yet graduated, or the computer major has graduated, then if there is enough time, I personally recommend self-study, this is the lowest efficiency and cost, and now a lot of offline online training institutions are actually very good, but the learning cost is high, the second investment time is more, the basic need to focus on training for 3-6 months.
However, if this is what I say, self-study is very convenient, many of the learning resources on the network are now free of charge, or there are a lot of training resources to B station, if you will not look for resources, you can also contact me through the introduction, get free resources, or detailed consultation.
In addition, there are some more classic books that can be combined with video comprehensive learning.
If you are not a computer professional, but can also pay a certain amount of learning money and time costs, then it is recommended to go to a training institution to study, so that the study does not have to be very laborious, the teacher's explanation is also very detailed, there are some special answers, in addition to learning planning or supervision is also helpful.
And now a large number of training institutions will sign an employment agreement, there will be a quota, after the study is recommended to go to the company, so that the interview process to find a job can also save a lot of things.
The above is some of my views, mentioned earlier because I do not understand your situation, so it is probably not detailed, if there are others who want to consult, you can contact me at any time to communicate.
