Yunnan: co-ordinating and standardizing the management of rural public welfare posts - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Kunming, December 12 (Reporter Lin Bifeng) In order to continue to do a good job in supporting the employment of poverty-stricken people and consolidate and expand the achievements of poverty alleviation, Yunnan Province has recently issued policies to promote the management of rural public welfare posts to help comprehensively promote rural rejuvenation.
According to the relevant person in charge of the Yunnan Provincial Human Resources and Social Security Department, at present, a total of 448,300 rural public welfare jobs have been developed in Yunnan, which is used to place the employment of rural difficult groups such as the poverty-stricken labor force, which plays an important role in helping the people out of poverty to increase employment, consolidate the achievements in poverty alleviation, and effectively improve the capacity of various public services in the countryside.
The new regulations are jointly issued by seven departments such as Yunnan human society, rural rejuvenation, and finance, and are mainly standardized on the target scope, fund management, job development, and post management for grass-roots recruitment.
In terms of job development settings, the new regulations are clearly set up in accordance with the principles of "on-the-demand placement, fixed personnel, dynamic management, total control", "who develops, who uses, who is responsible" and "one person, one post, voluntary open, unified management".
The recruitment process must be carried out in accordance with the steps such as announcements, declarations, audits, publicity, recruitment, pre-service training and placement.
In addition, the new regulations also clarifies the specific responsibilities of the main development departments of rural public welfare posts, subsidy standards and subsidy methods for rural public welfare posts, and stipulates that the rural public welfare job development departments should purchase accidental injury commercial insurance for rural public welfare job placement personnel; the relevant departments are required to regularly supervise the issuance of subsidies for rural public welfare posts.
