The starry sky, the Geminid meteor shower on the 14th ushered in a great - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency, Tianjin, December 12 (Reporter Zhou Runjian) astronomical popular science experts said that as the last large-scale meteor shower of the year, one of the three major meteor showers in the northern hemisphere, the Geminid meteor shower, will be very large on December 14, and friends who like meteor showers can observe in the middle of the night.
The Geminid meteor shower was photographed in Qinghai on December 13, 2018.
The parent body of most meteor showers are periodic comets, but the parent body of the Geminid meteor shower is asteroid 3200, which is an Apollo-type asteroid.
The Geminid meteor shower is also the second known meteor shower that is not "bred" by a comet.
Xiu Lippeng, director of the Tianjin Astronomical Society and an expert in astronomical popular science, said that just like New Year's blockbusters, the Geminid meteor shower generally appears at the end of the year, and the "radiation period" can last from December 4th to the 17th.
The meteor shower is known for its large and stable flow and, together with the quadrant meteor shower and the Perseid meteor shower, is known as the three major meteor showers in the northern hemisphere.
A significant feature of the Geminid meteor shower is that the meteoroid speed is slow, rich in color, there are a lot of fiery meteors, which are suitable for both visuals and beginners in astrophotography.
The Geminid meteor shower photographed by Tianjin astronomy enthusiast Yang Jing on December 13, 2020 in Jingzhou, Tianjin.
According to the astronomical forecast, this year's Geminid meteor shower will be extremely large at about 15:00 on December 14th, with a maximum ZHR (the number of meteors that can be seen per hour when the radiation point is directly above the head under ideal observation conditions).
The Geminid meteor shower recommended index chart.
â€œLast year â€œdaughty and colorful' Geminid meteor shower made a deep impression on people, but this year's Geminid meteor shower will be disturbed by moonlight, the degree will be a little discount.
On the 11th day of the lunar calendar on November 11th, the lunar phase is a convex moon, and the bright moonlight will interfere with the observation, so that the moon will fall in the middle of the night, at which time the radiant point of the Geminid meteor shower will also rise relatively high.
Friends who like meteor showers can observe these few hours after midnight, but they should pay attention to cold and keep warm."
How do we see as many meteors as possible?
It is not recommended to make observations in the city, you can choose a high-altitude, light damage, north-nor-thirty view in the suburbs or villages, and then patiently wait until the moon falls, visual observation can be.
It should be noted that the Geminid meteor shower has a very large flow in all directions, and it is not necessary to keep staring at the radiant points of the Geminid meteor shower during observation.
Friends who like photography want to shoot a gorgeous "meteor shower blockbuster", it is best to choose a wide-angle, large aperture lens, the use of high ISO and the maximum aperture when shooting.
Tripods, spare batteries and shutter lines are also essential based on stability and continuity considerations.”
