What's the difference between laser TV and traditional TV in terms of market positioning?
According to my understanding, the traditional TV should refer to the LCD TV, and the difference between laser TV and LCD TV in the market positioning, there are mainly the following two points:
First, the laser TV is more focused on the large-screen market.
Compared with the comprehensive market positioning of LCD TVs, laser TVs are obviously more focused on the large-screen market, or laser TV itself is the product of large screens.
At present, the mainstream LCD TV size is more than 55 inches to 65 inches, while the size of the laser TV is generally more than 75 inches, the largest is more than 100 inches, to fully meet the needs of users for large-screen color TVs.
In recent years, the proportion of laser TV shipments and sales in the world has been increasing, accounting for more than 60% of the overall TV sales of 80 inches and above.
According to the forecast, in 2020, the sales volume of the laser TV market will increase by more than 140%, and it will continue to maintain rapid growth.
The reason why there are such good results in the large-screen market is mainly due to the excellent performance of laser TV in eye protection.
Based on the imaging principle of laser TV diffuse reflection, the light emitted by the laser light source is not directed into the eye, compared with the backlight of the LCD TV, the imaging process is closer to the imaging process of the objects under natural conditions, and the stimulation to the eyes is also smaller.
China Electronic Technology Standardization Research Institute Sisi laboratory and Beijing Union Hospital ophthalmology experts, through the crowd under the same conditions to watch the laser TV and LCD TV strict comparison test, came up with 144 sets of test data.
The data confirm that laser TV does have a very strong eye protection characteristics and even has a certain improvement effect in specific aspects.
At a time when vision health is becoming more and more important, laser TV has not only attracted more and more users with eye protection advantages, but also opened another breakthrough in the color TV market.
Second, laser TV is more focused on the high-end market.
Contrary to the continuous decline in the prices of LCD TVs, the current price of commercial laser TV is mostly more than ten thousand yuan, and with the upgrading of size and light source, the price is gradually rising.
Why are laser TVs so expensive?
It certainly makes sense.
With the continuous development of light sources and technical level, laser TVs have many advantages that can not be achieved with LCD TVs and projections.
With ultra-short focal length projection technology, the projection distance of the laser TV is relatively shorter than that of traditional projection equipment, which can achieve a 100-inch large-screen experience within a short distance, the required space is not large, and the host is very small and occupies a very small place.
In terms of brilliance, large brands of laser TVs can reach more than 2,000 lumens.
In addition, the heat is lower, the equipment loss is small, and the service life of the TV is even longer.
In addition, many high-end laser TV models are also equipped with many cutting-edge technologies such as real 4K ultra-high-definition image quality, artificial intelligence systems, and bionic screens, which can give users a more shocking audio-visual experience.
It does not talk about pseudo-demand, but the product of demand subdivision, the picture quality and input-output ratio, laser TV is not the dish of the video player, want to take into account the lack of large screen and viewing environment, you can try, everything has pros and cons, after weighing your own judgment, you are afraid to listen to a word of faith.
Simply put, the ultra-wide-angle near-focus projector - laser TV, in order to be close to the screen, had to use expensive ultra-wide-angle lenses and reflectors, which does not meet the best optical design.
In order to shield part of the ambient light, the use of the micro-structure of the fisser screen is expensive, and the price of 80 inches can basically be replaced by a 65-inch liquid crystal.
Another point, I especially hate projection manufacturers to take diffuse reflection to the eyes of this as a selling point, please, the eyes can see the light on the screen for the eyes is direct light, you diffuse reflected to the ceiling, the eyes can not be seen, have to be more than the real LCD TV is also long "straight, open the TV ceiling will not also be illuminated?"
In addition, the projection screen, if it is not a diffuse reflection, it does not look like at all.
It's just that the hot spot (light spot) effect of the high-gain screen is ignored, and a large amount of light is reflected to the eyes at a certain angle, which is really uncomfortable.
