Sino-Vietnamese military "peace and rescue-2021" joint exercise was successfully concluded - Xinhua
On the morning of the 12th, the Chinese participating detachments participating in the Sino-Vietnamese "Peaceful Rescue-2021" health and service joint exercise between the two militaries were safely returned to the territory of Guangxi, China, marking the successful completion of the seven-day training mission.
In this joint exercise, the Sino-Vietnamese two militaries focused on the major issue of humanitarian medical rescue, closely linked to the task of saving lives and injuries, and in accordance with the actual combat standards to complete the contents of the joint health service command, joint on-the-spot rescue, and the disposal of the injured in bulk, effectively improving the security capabilities of the two militaries.
The results of the exercise have been confirmed by the two militaries.
At the end-of-the-up ceremony, the director of the Vietnam-Vietnam People’s Exercise Steering Committee and deputy director and chief of staff of the Vietnam People’s Army General Nguyen Xuan Sheng said at the end of the exercise that through this exercise, Vietnamese military doctors learned about the organization and professional activities of the exercises from Chinese military doctors, as well as seeing China’s medical and security equipment.
The results of the exercise proved the professional ability of the military medical forces of the two countries in terms of medical assistance and epidemic prevention and control.
Chen Chunming, leader of the Chinese guiding coordination group and deputy director of the Health Bureau of the Logistics Support Department of the Central Military Commission, said that the exercise is another pioneering and innovative practice on the basis of the successful holding of joint clinics in 2018, which is of a very important milestone significance.
During the exercise, the Chinese People's Liberation Army donated medical protective masks, medical protective clothing, rapid nucleic acid detection instruments and other health and anti-epidemic materials to the Vietnamese People's Army.
